---
// design/11_PRESS.md, ui_ux/11_PRESS_UI.md. Hidden from nav (Nav.astro has never included it)
// and excluded from the sitemap — sitemap generation itself is a Block 5 task; flagging here so
// whoever wires it in remembers to exclude this route explicitly.
//
// VENUE: "AAAI 2027" appears twice in design/11's source (the one-page brief, and PR-001's
// headline/body). Same site-wide correction as Home/Footer/Paper — omitted until the AAAI
// anonymity check clears (design/12 §Pre-Launch Checklist).
//
// TBD PLACEHOLDERS, not resolved (per this task's own instruction — these are pending
// decisions, not copy gaps): the location line, and PR-002's partner name/finding summary.
// Each renders with the visible amber-ghost/amber-mid-border treatment ui_ux/11 §2 specifies,
// so a missing variable reads as a missing variable, not as finished copy.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../components/Eyebrow.astro';
---

<Page title="PRESS">
	<section class="section container press-page">
		<Eyebrow>PRESS</Eyebrow>
		<h1>Press</h1>
		<p class="press-prose">
			Materials for journalists, analysts, and researchers covering Oxiedo. All factual
			claims on this page are sourced and verifiable. We will respond to press inquiries
			within a few days — usually less.
		</p>
		<p class="press-contact">
			Press contact: [REPLACE WITH DOMAIN EMAIL BEFORE LAUNCH]<br />
			Subject line: "Press inquiry — [outlet name]"
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal press-page">
		<h2>The one-page brief</h2>
		<p class="press-prose">
			<strong>What Oxiedo is:</strong> Oxiedo is building on a single architectural
			discovery: bounding each node of a neural network's local gradient chain to four
			operations makes that node independently addressable. The company calls this property
			"addressability." It enables a new class of commercial solutions — the first of which
			are ready to engage today.
		</p>
		<p class="press-prose">
			<strong>The technology:</strong> The ORMAS architecture (Orchestrated Repair and
			Monitoring with Architectural Self-correction) emits a five-layer telemetry stack as a
			physical byproduct of training — not as post-hoc analysis. Results across 383
			controlled experiments show:
		</p>
		<ul class="press-list">
			<li>
				80.3% recovery from mid-training structural collapse where a standard network
				permanently collapsed to 10% (+70.3 pp gap)
			</li>
			<li>94.6% task retention after sequential shift, no replay buffer, no task ID (baseline: 47.3%)</li>
			<li>58.8% zero-shot compositional accuracy on unseen combinations (baseline: 25%)</li>
			<li>−2.5 pp degradation under 40% label noise (baseline: −7.8 pp)</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="press-prose">All results: CIFAR-10 / CIFAR-100. Manuscript under review.</p>
		<p class="press-prose">
			<strong>The solutions:</strong> The Warning Light is available for immediate
			engagement. The Proofreader (label quality analysis) and The Diary (compliance record)
			are in active build and open for Charter Partnership pre-booking. Four more are in
			development, pending V2 completion and one validation study.
		</p>
		<p class="press-prose">
			<strong>The company:</strong> Founded by Rokib Al Dhin Raadh, an independent
			researcher. Engine MIT-licensed. Repository will be public after the review period.
			Pre-revenue. Not yet venture-backed. Based in <span class="press-tbd">LOCATION TBD — add before press outreach begins</span>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal press-page">
		<h2>Press releases (prepared, not released)</h2>
		<p class="press-prose">These are drafted but on hold. They are stored here for when each event occurs.</p>

		<div class="press-release">
			<p class="press-release-status tabular">PR-001 · STATUS: READY TO RELEASE when manuscript is formally accepted.</p>
			<p class="press-release-headline">
				Oxiedo Publishes Research Architecture That Lets Neural Networks Keep a Record of
				What They Change
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose">
				383-Experiment Evidence Base Shows +70.3 pp Recovery Advantage Over Standard
				Networks Under Mid-Training Structural Collapse
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose">
				Oxiedo today released the full research foundation for its training architecture,
				ORMAS (Orchestrated Repair and Monitoring with Architectural Self-correction), via
				a submitted manuscript.
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose">
				The architecture bounds each node's local gradient chain to four operations,
				producing per-node attribution as a physical property of the backward pass — not
				as a reconstruction. Across 383 controlled experiments on CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100,
				the system demonstrated 80.3% recovery from mid-training structural collapse
				compared to a permanent 10.0% for parameter-matched standard networks, a gap of
				+70.3 percentage points.
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose-note">(Full boilerplate, quote from founder, and assets to be added at release.)</p>
		</div>

		<div class="press-release">
			<p class="press-release-status tabular">
				PR-002 · STATUS: HOLD — release when first external engagement is complete and
				partner approves.
			</p>
			<p class="press-release-headline">
				Oxiedo Completes First External Diagnostic: <span class="press-tbd">PARTNER NAME</span>
				<span class="press-tbd">FINDING SUMMARY</span>
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose-note">(Template — fill in specifics.)</p>
		</div>

		<div class="press-release">
			<p class="press-release-status tabular">PR-003 · STATUS: HOLD — release if/when separation study passes.</p>
			<p class="press-release-headline">
				Oxiedo Confirms Central V2 Premise: Architecture Separates Mislabelled Data from
				Hard Examples Reliably
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose-note">(Template — add exact results.)</p>
		</div>

		<div class="press-release">
			<p class="press-release-status tabular">PR-004 · STATUS: HOLD — release if separation study fails.</p>
			<p class="press-release-headline">Oxiedo Reports Separation Study Result and Updates Solution Roadmap</p>
			<p class="press-prose">
				The source-attribution validation study returned <span class="press-tbd">result</span>.
				Four solutions as previously described are removed from the roadmap. The Warning
				Light, The Proofreader, and The Diary are unaffected. Updated roadmap available at
				oxiedo.com/solutions.
			</p>
			<p class="press-prose-note">
				Note: having PR-004 already written is itself a signal. Companies that have a
				press release ready for their downside case are companies a journalist can trust.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal press-page">
		<h2>Assets</h2>
		<ul class="press-list">
			<li>Logo (SVG) — full colour</li>
			<li>Logo (SVG) — white on transparent</li>
			<li>Logo (PNG) — 1200px</li>
			<li>Founder photo (if available)</li>
			<li>Solution diagram — the four operations</li>
			<li>Market map diagram — five sectors</li>
			<li>Architecture diagram — three signals + telemetry stack</li>
			<li>Press brief (PDF, one page)</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal press-page">
		<h2>Boilerplate</h2>
		<p class="press-prose">
			Oxiedo is building on the ORMAS architecture (Orchestrated Repair and Monitoring with
			Architectural Self-correction), a neural network design that makes per-node causal
			attribution a physical property of training — enabling per-component diagnosis,
			bounded structural treatment, audit, and deletion of data contributions in trained
			models. All corrections are logged, bounded, and human-reviewable. The architecture is
			submitted for peer review, with 383 controlled experiments across four architecture
			families. The engine is MIT-licensed. The repository will be made public after the
			review period ends.
		</p>
		<p class="press-prose">
			All experimental results are CIFAR-10 / CIFAR-100. No clinical, biological, financial,
			or production data has been used. The Warning Light is available for immediate
			engagement. The Proofreader and The Diary are in active build and open for Charter
			Partnership pre-booking. Oxiedo is pre-revenue and unfunded as of September 2026.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section container reveal press-page">
		<h2>Corrections policy</h2>
		<p class="press-prose">If you believe a claim on this site or in a press release is inaccurate:</p>
		<p class="press-prose">
			Contact [REPLACE WITH DOMAIN EMAIL BEFORE LAUNCH] with "Correction — [specific claim]"
			in the subject line. Every claim on this site is sourced. We will respond with the
			source or issue a correction.
		</p>
		<p class="press-prose">We do not have a PR agency. You will receive a response from the founder.</p>
	</section>
</Page>
